"Authority is the ability to impress one's desires upon everything: the essence of magic."
"The Artonan word also translates as dominion or influence; English has no ideal word."
"Artonans feel authority from birth as a sixth sense and train it like a muscle."
"Most species cannot sense authority; humans often mistake it for willpower."
"When two authorities conflict, the stronger wins, even a mother tree over an Avowed."
"Rank correlates heavily with authority."
"A person's own authority can appear as a cobwebby cocoon wrapped around them."
"Overextending beyond one's authority, as the grandiose do, leaves a skill unenforceable."
"Magic works through perception nudging authority, skills binding it, conscious control, or rituals."
"Magic is less one science than sciences, arts and arcana handed down from long-dead wizards."
"Avowed almost never awaken a sense of their own authority unaided."
"Pushed too far out of alignment, authority stops recovering and chaos breaks in."
"Newborn wizards' authority senses are coddled; an adult could smoosh them."
"Skills that target a person give a mild poke to the target's authority, unfelt by most."
